Track 3: Reliquary for a Frequency No Longer Broadcast
- Story & Context: The closer begins with Noah playing a recorded station-identification tone found on an old maintenance cassette, but it is used only once and never looped. Clara searches for a tromba-marina harmonic near the remembered pitch and deliberately leaves the small beating difference audible. The track settles into 92 BPM with brushed snare, soft kick, fretless pedal, and sparse electric-piano fifths.

Mateu plays his longest phrase on the EP, still muted and restrained, moving through four notes that trace the contour of the obsolete station signal without quoting it literally. Clara answers each brass phrase with a different harmonic node, making the old transmission seem to migrate from circuitry into wood and string.

In the final section, Noah removes the drum machine, then Rhodes, then all tape processing. Irene sustains one low fretless note while Leila reduces to fingertips on frame-drum skin. Mateu lowers the horn. Clara continues alone, bowing the closest available harmonic to the original test tone until bow pressure weakens and the bridge buzz becomes louder than the pitch itself. She stops. The final sound is the tiny mechanical settling of the bridge foot against the instrument body.
